00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:36.540
The big reveal at the end of The Nun is that
Frenchie's real name is Maurice, and that

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.719
he's the French-Canadian farmer whose exorcism
the Warrens discussed during their lecture

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:42.450
in the first Conjuring movie.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:43.450
"Take Maurice here.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.950
A French-Canadian farmer with no more than
a third-grade education..

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:50.530
..yet, after he was possessed, spoke some
of the best Latin I'd ever heard.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:51.530
Sometimes backwards.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.940
A dark spirit made its home in this man."

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:59.179
"And like that.. ..an upside down cross started
to appear from within his body."

00:00:59.179 --> 00:01:03.129
At the end of The Nun, we see the origins
of that cross inside Maurice's body via the

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.790
upside-down cross that's revealed on the back
of Frenchie's neck.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:11.190
We also see that during the final fight with
Valak, the demon Nun vomited a snake into

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.620
Frenchie's mouth.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:17.100
The demon Valak has a number of names, one
of which is "the Marquis of Snakes" meaning

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:21.760
he has the power to summon and command snakes,
which suggests that the snake Valak put into

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.320
Frenchie means the demon possessed him or
can control him.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.210
In fact, the movie's director Corin Hardy
has described Frenchie as the film's "secret

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:33.570
weapon" and it's interesting that in The Nun,
Frenchie works as a delivery man to the abbey

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:38.100
which is a neat bit of foreshadowing for how
many years later Maurice delivers that horrifying

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.610
vision of Valak to Lorraine.

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:42.100
"I had a vision in Amityville.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:47.160
It was the same one I had seven years ago.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:53.320
I had a premonition of your death."

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:57.140
In a similar way to how the Church closed
the gateway to Hell at the time of the Duke,

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:00.840
at the end of the film, the portal in the
convent is closed when the blood of Christ

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.180
spills into the pool of water on top of the
opening.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:08.610
Sister Irene appears to have defeated Valak
when she spits holy blood all over the demon

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:12.580
which seems to send him back to Hell via the
gateway in the convent's floor, but it looks

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:16.550
like she was a little too late as right at
the end it appears that Maurice is now the

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.280
vessel for Valak to escape.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:23.000
That ending was foreshadowed near the start
of the film when Frenchie told Sister Irene

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.590
that the locals always spit when the castle
is mentioned in order "to ward off evil".

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:31.620
And although Frenchie said it was "an old
and silly superstition", he spat on the ground

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.560
himself before entering the castle for the
first time.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.890
James Wan has already said he has a potential
story in mind for a Nun sequel which would

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:42.950
come back to Lorraine's story in the two Conjuring
movies so far.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:48.150
Which means a Nun sequel could explore how
Valak returns via Maurice and could also illuminate

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.980
just why the demon is so interested in the
Warrens.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:56.180
OK, so we need to talk in some more detail
about Sister Irene and how the movie teases

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:59.100
a number of connections between her and Lorraine
Warren.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.180
First, there's the interesting coincidence
that Taissa Farmiga, who plays Irene, is the

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:06.280
real-life sister of Vera Farmiga who plays
Lorraine.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:12.590
Taissa is around 21 years younger than Vera
and with The Nun set in 1952, about 19 years

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:17.400
before The Conjuring and 25 years before its
sequel, it seems possible there could be some

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.870
kind of family connection between Irene and
Lorraine that might be revealed in the next

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:24.040
Nun or Conjuring movie.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:27.940
And although during set visits for The Nun,
cast and crew said there's no connection,

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:31.910
they could just be trying to keep things under
wraps or give themselves time to figure out

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:34.610
exactly how that'll work in a sequel.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:39.060
Character-wise, Irene's visions and premonitions
are similar to Lorraine's psychic abilities

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:42.930
and could point to their being related by
blood or otherwise connected.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:47.460
Then there's a very interesting parallel in
how the demonic nun reveals itself to both

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.319
Irene and Lorraine.

00:03:49.319 --> 00:03:54.220
Valak manifests itself to Irene via a mirror
during one of Irene's visions in a similar

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:59.160
way to how we see Lorraine's vision of the
demon in a mirror during her Amityville séance.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:03.910
The Nun movie also echoes the scene from The
Conjuring 2 where the demon nun's shadow crawls

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:09.160
along a wall before physically appearing in
the painting of the Nun where it attacks Lorraine.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:13.550
In this movie, the nun's shadow crawls along
the chapel wall before appearing in the mirror

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.100
behind Irene.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.810
On top of that, during Maurice's exorcism
which we see at the end of The Nun, the way

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:23.599
he grabs and looks at Lorraine makes me wonder
if he senses a connection between her and

00:04:23.599 --> 00:04:28.409
Irene who he knew from Romania or, perhaps
in his terror, he mistook Lorraine for Irene,

00:04:28.409 --> 00:04:32.729
or maybe it's actually Valak who feels the
connection between the two women.

00:04:32.729 --> 00:04:36.550
There's also an Annabelle: Creation easter
egg in The Nun when we get to see again the

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:41.009
photograph of Sister Charlotte with three
nuns and Valak that she showed to Mr Mullins

00:04:41.009 --> 00:04:42.979
in the Annabelle prequel movie.

00:04:42.979 --> 00:04:44.430
"That's sister Maria.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:45.560
That's sister Anna.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:48.150
And that's sister Lucia."

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.439
"Who's this?"

00:04:49.439 --> 00:04:51.379
"I... don't know.

00:04:51.379 --> 00:04:55.900
I don't think I even met her."

00:04:55.900 --> 00:05:00.949
I was wondering if we might actually meet
Sisters Maria, Anna and Lucia, but the fact

00:05:00.949 --> 00:05:04.580
they were never mentioned in the Nun movie
makes me think they probably perished at the

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:07.650
hands of Valak before Sister Irene arrived.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:12.289
Like in The Conjuring 2, The Nun also packs
a number of hidden Valak words into the background

00:05:12.289 --> 00:05:13.300
of the movie.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:17.819
The first one I noticed is that Valak's name
is hidden in the window frame of Sister Victoria's

00:05:17.819 --> 00:05:18.819
room.

00:05:18.819 --> 00:05:23.740
You can also see "Valak" in part of the periodic
table on the classroom wall, and it also appears

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:29.939
as "VA01 LAK" on the luggage truck's license
plate; in addition to that, it's hidden among

00:05:29.939 --> 00:05:31.580
the trees of the forest.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:36.540
Right, now it's time to talk about that big
twist that occurs when Irene is keeping vigil

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:37.669
in the chapel.

00:05:37.669 --> 00:05:41.629
She sees nuns walk in to the chapel to pray
with her to keep Valak at bay but later they're

00:05:41.629 --> 00:05:43.999
all tossed aside by the demonic force.

00:05:43.999 --> 00:05:49.190
As Sister Irene continues to pray in an attempt
to hold back the evil power, Valak slices

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:50.770
a "V" into her exposed shoulders.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:55.930
The carving continues turning the "V" into
a pentagram, marking Irene and foreshadowing

00:05:55.930 --> 00:06:00.440
how Valak will later trick her and lead her
into a pentagram, finally possessing her before

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:05.059
Frenchie places holy blood on her face to
cast out the demon and bring her back.

00:06:05.059 --> 00:06:09.409
Visually this is an impressive scene; however,
what happens next turns our understanding

00:06:09.409 --> 00:06:14.870
of the movie upside down when Sister Irene
realises that none of the nuns were ever really

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:16.069
there with her.

00:06:16.069 --> 00:06:20.569
And at that point, it seems like all of Irene's
interactions with the nuns have just been

00:06:20.569 --> 00:06:22.529
visions or spirits.

00:06:22.529 --> 00:06:27.210
This revelation links back to the opening
scene of the movie where Sister Victoria committed

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.210
suicide.

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:32.270
It seems like Victoria knew she was the last
surviving nun at the convent which is why

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:37.659
she knew she had to sacrifice herself so that
Valak couldn't take her soul and use her as

00:06:37.659 --> 00:06:39.300
"a vessel to escape."

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:44.339
And peppered through the movie are clues hinting
that the convent is empty of any living nuns.

00:06:44.339 --> 00:06:48.409
For example, the Abbess – who is dead herself
– won't let anyone into the convent when

00:06:48.409 --> 00:06:51.940
they arrive and only Irene is allowed in the
next day.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:56.569
Also, initially when Irene finds Sister Oana
dead in the chapel it looks like she's only

00:06:56.569 --> 00:07:02.470
just died, however after Irene's vision disappears,
Oana's body is still there but it's very dark

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:07.669
and seems to be decomposing suggesting Oana's
actually been dead for some time.

00:07:07.669 --> 00:07:12.009
Which indicates that Irene's conversations
with Oana were not with a living nun but rather

00:07:12.009 --> 00:07:15.369
they were visions or appearances of Oana's
spirit.

00:07:15.369 --> 00:07:20.240
It's possible many of these visions have been
a trick by Valak to weaken Irene psychologically

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:24.059
and prepare her to be possessed when she unknowingly
walks into the pentagram.

00:07:24.059 --> 00:07:29.729
Basically, Valak has been taking her through
the three stages of demonic activity: infestation,

00:07:29.729 --> 00:07:31.889
oppression, and finally possession.

00:07:31.889 --> 00:07:36.810
A narrative thread left open at the end of
the movie is Father Burke's wounded eye which

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:40.830
he suffered when the ghost of Daniel attacked
Burke with his serpent tongue which latched

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.909
itself on to the Father's eye.

00:07:42.909 --> 00:07:46.490
Daniel was the boy who died when Burke tried
to exorcise him.

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:50.869
Although Burke eventually gets away, I wonder
whether he was infected in any way similar

00:07:50.869 --> 00:07:52.740
to what happened to Frenchie.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:57.469
Overall, the plot of The Nun seems more complicated
and ambiguous than it needs to be and although

00:07:57.469 --> 00:08:01.229
I've laid out my understanding of the twist
based on my initial viewing, I can see there's

00:08:01.229 --> 00:08:02.530
room for different interpretations.

